<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine peso ends weaker on central bank cue.</title>
<headline>Philippine peso ends weaker on central bank cue.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------- Feb 5 -------------------------</p>
<p>		 * Thin turnover at $118 million</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The Philippine peso closed slightly weaker at 26.340 to the dollar from Tuesday's close of 26.331 after the central bank lifted its selling price to 26.345 from 26.340 earlier in the day, traders said.</p>
<p>One trader said the market was just coasting along with the central bank's day-to-day strategy, although he added that banks were seeing a peso depreciating trend.</p>
</text>
